# Build output
node_modules/
dist/
.test-build/
.esbuild-tmp/
.tmp/
.e2e-workspace/
.wv2-data/
.webview-data/
render-check.png
render-check-light.png

# The throwaway production bundle `scripts/stream-perf.mjs` measures against: a
# real production build with the harness handles kept
# (`VITE_PERF_HARNESS=true npx vite build --outDir .perf-build`). It cannot be
# `dist/`, because the numbers are only meaningful from a bundle with the
# dev-only double render and prop validation compiled out, and a plain
# `npm run build` has the handles stripped. Build output either way.
.perf-build/

# A WebView2/IME subprocess drops this next to whatever directory the app was
# launched from. It is not our output.
debug.log

# Scratch logs from driving the window by hand while chasing the launch failure
# the README records. Diagnostics from one machine, not part of the program.
launch.log
probe-launch.log

# Tauri build logs, from scripts/build-installer.ps1 and any manual run.
.tauri-build*.log
.tudouni-tauri-build.log

# Rust
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# The staged runtime: an 18 MB binary plus a 4 MB ripgrep, both regenerated by
# `make release`. Committing them would let them drift from VERSION.
# Run `npm run runtime:stage` to populate this directory.
src-tauri/runtime/*
!src-tauri/runtime/README.md

# The staged remote install archives: the **packed** releases for every shipped
# platform, which the Remote Bootstrapper uploads over SFTP. Build output, the
# same way `runtime/` is — each one is ~9 MB and regenerated by
# `npm run runtime:stage-remote` from `dist/` after `make release`. Committing
# them would let them drift from VERSION, and would put 19 MB of binaries in the
# history for every release.
#
# `tauri.conf.json` lists `remote-packages/*.zip` as a bundle resource, so a
# packaged build **does** carry them; they are simply not version-controlled.
#
# The pattern excludes the *archives* rather than the directory, because git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded — and the
# directory itself has to be committable for its README (which explains how to
# populate it) to be tracked at all. `runtime/` above uses the same shape.
src-tauri/remote-packages/*
!src-tauri/remote-packages/README.md

# TypeScript incremental build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Mobile icon sets: this project ships Windows (NSIS) and Linux only.
# Regenerated by: npx tauri icon src-tauri/icons/source-icon.png -o src-tauri/icons
src-tauri/icons/android/
src-tauri/icons/ios/
